# Root build-context .dockerignore (WR-01 belt-and-suspenders, Phase 118).
#
# The frontend image builds (admin-app, client-pwa) use the repo root as their
# build context. The per-Dockerfile ignore files at
# infra/docker/<name>.Dockerfile.dockerignore are honored by BuildKit, but the
# legacy builder only ever reads THIS root .dockerignore. Keeping the same
# exclusions here guarantees host node_modules (macOS-native binaries), dist
# output, git/planning metadata, and .env files never enter the build context
# regardless of which builder runs — preventing build corruption and ~1.2GB of
# context bloat.
#
# NOTE: the backend image builds with context apps/backend/ (NOT repo root), so
# this file does not affect it — apps/backend/.dockerignore covers that build.

# Local dependency installs (reinstalled fresh inside the build container)
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Existing build output (produced inside the container, not copied from host)
apps/admin-app/dist/
apps/client-pwa/dist/
**/dist/

# Backend source (not needed for frontend builds)
apps/backend/

# Test and tooling artifacts
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/coverage/
**/htmlcov/
**/.coverage

# Git and editor metadata
.git/
.gitignore
**/.gitkeep

# Planning and docs
.planning/
*.md
**/CLAUDE.md

# Environment files (never in build context — T-118-03)
**/.env*

# TypeScript build info (stale artifacts)
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Design assets (not needed for production builds)
apps/admin-app/design/
apps/client-pwa/plans/

# Local worktrees / agent scratch (must never enter a build context)
.claude/
